WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.826 --> 00:00:04.760
- So, we're gonna be handcuffed together

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.549
for the next 24 hours.

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:07.909
- What the hell is this?

00:00:07.909 --> 00:00:10.492
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.536 --> 00:00:15.437
So, a little backstory a
lot of people don't know

00:00:15.437 --> 00:00:18.117
is we didn't grow up
in the same household,

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.988
so for us to have only really spent

00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:24.632
as much as a summer or
a Christmas together,

00:00:24.632 --> 00:00:26.867
we kind of keep in touch pretty well,

00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:29.586
considering that gap in our lives.

00:00:29.586 --> 00:00:30.846
But we come together,

00:00:30.846 --> 00:00:33.498
and now we're handcuffed
together for an entire day.

00:00:33.498 --> 00:00:36.213
I had just set up everything
I was gonna do for work

00:00:36.213 --> 00:00:38.914
and you go, "We're out."

00:00:38.914 --> 00:00:40.998
The gate clicker's in my car.

00:00:40.998 --> 00:00:42.796
- Which means we have
to get out of this car?

00:00:42.796 --> 00:00:44.295
- That means we have to get back out.

00:00:44.295 --> 00:00:45.274
- And then back in?

00:00:45.274 --> 00:00:47.357
- And then back in, yeah.

00:00:54.245 --> 00:00:55.078
- So, I'm hungry.

00:00:55.078 --> 00:00:55.911
- [Michael] Is it--

00:00:55.911 --> 00:00:57.495
- Let's go get some food.

00:00:57.495 --> 00:00:58.328
All right.

00:00:58.328 --> 00:00:59.955
After that, we went to Chipotle.

00:00:59.955 --> 00:01:01.034
(Michael laughs)

00:01:01.034 --> 00:01:02.878
And then we get to
Chipotle and we're in line,

00:01:02.878 --> 00:01:05.594
and this lady was like, "Oof, rough day?"

00:01:05.594 --> 00:01:07.540
- It was only 45 minutes in.
- It's that bad.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.373
- She could already see
it all over our faces.

00:01:08.373 --> 00:01:09.336
- She could see what was happening!

00:01:09.336 --> 00:01:10.372
- She completely,

00:01:10.372 --> 00:01:12.078
I mean, but when you walk
into a food establishment

00:01:12.078 --> 00:01:13.236
with handcuffs on--
- True.

00:01:13.236 --> 00:01:14.524
- Something is off.

00:01:14.524 --> 00:01:15.636
You can tell everybody

00:01:15.636 --> 00:01:17.164
about the years of torment
that I put you through.

00:01:17.164 --> 00:01:19.132
- So, we are actually half-siblings,

00:01:19.132 --> 00:01:22.041
but I never got to see you very often,

00:01:22.041 --> 00:01:25.532
and so I would always be
this close to you. (laughs)

00:01:25.532 --> 00:01:27.368
- And when we got together,

00:01:27.368 --> 00:01:28.705
because of that--
- I really,

00:01:28.705 --> 00:01:31.392
I remember one time, you tried
to push me down the stairs.

00:01:31.392 --> 00:01:32.636
- I won't deny that.

00:01:32.636 --> 00:01:34.418
I also won't agree that that's true.

00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:36.924
- But we went from Chipotle,
and then we went to Sephora.

00:01:36.924 --> 00:01:39.468
Michael's girlfriend, Chhavi, was with us,

00:01:39.468 --> 00:01:41.257
and she really wanted
to go to buy Sephora,

00:01:41.257 --> 00:01:43.103
and I was like, "Hell
yeah, I'm down for it."

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.465
Mike is not feelin' this.

00:01:44.465 --> 00:01:45.632
It'll be okay.

00:01:46.891 --> 00:01:49.023
- But see, it's a lot--
- My place is there.

00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:51.458
Outside the door, where it's
comfortable and there's air.

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:52.805
- I tapped out.

00:01:52.805 --> 00:01:55.325
Chhavi wins, Chhavi definitely wins.

00:01:55.325 --> 00:01:57.178
It's only been two hours

00:01:57.178 --> 00:01:59.894
and this has been the
longest two hours of my life.

00:01:59.894 --> 00:02:01.015
- Feels like it's been 20.

00:02:01.015 --> 00:02:03.478
- When we were leaving
Sephora, Mike decided,

00:02:03.478 --> 00:02:05.850
out of the blue, he needed to take a leak.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.618
- I have to go to the bathroom.

00:02:07.618 --> 00:02:10.982
I have to go now, and it's right there.

00:02:10.982 --> 00:02:13.204
I'm not gonna lie to you,
it was kind of a spike pee.

00:02:13.204 --> 00:02:14.976
At that point, we were already in Sephora,

00:02:14.976 --> 00:02:16.642
(laughs) and I was just like,
- What?

00:02:16.642 --> 00:02:18.348
- "I'm lettin' it rip."

00:02:18.348 --> 00:02:19.181
- [Destinee] I'm talkin' bout,

00:02:19.181 --> 00:02:20.507
I walked in there with like head down,

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:22.682
I was like, "Okay, I'm just
gonna look at my feet."

00:02:22.682 --> 00:02:24.902
- And this one guy was like
starin' at you the whole time.

00:02:24.902 --> 00:02:26.178
Like it kinda creeped me out.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:28.518
He saw you walk in as he
was about to walk out,

00:02:28.518 --> 00:02:30.418
and he was like, "No, I'm here for this."

00:02:30.418 --> 00:02:32.394
- (laughs) And we went to the nail salon

00:02:32.394 --> 00:02:34.681
and they were very accommodating.

00:02:34.681 --> 00:02:35.514
- [Michael] They were.

00:02:35.514 --> 00:02:36.378
- [Destinee] They gave us a pillow,

00:02:36.378 --> 00:02:37.862
they gave him a stool to sit next to me.

00:02:37.862 --> 00:02:38.758
- [Michael] They were very nice.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:39.874
- They also said, "What
the hell are you doing?"

00:02:39.874 --> 00:02:40.707
(both laugh)

00:02:40.707 --> 00:02:41.540
- Yeah.

00:02:44.566 --> 00:02:45.434
- Sorry.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:46.267
- And we were kinda,

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:47.698
we were kinda good about
going back and forth.

00:02:47.698 --> 00:02:49.850
- It'll be fine! (laughs)

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.802
Come on, let's go! (laughs)

00:02:52.802 --> 00:02:55.142
Michael, come on, I'm serious!

00:02:55.142 --> 00:02:59.214
(laughing) Mike, Mike, Mike!

00:02:59.214 --> 00:03:03.131
Okay, okay, you win, you
win, you win, you win!

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.247
(Michael laughs)

00:03:07.247 --> 00:03:09.107
- But then my blood sugar
started getting low.

00:03:09.107 --> 00:03:10.307
I got real hungry.

00:03:10.307 --> 00:03:11.807
- That was by the time we
got to the grocery store.

00:03:11.807 --> 00:03:13.124
By the time we got to the grocery store,

00:03:13.124 --> 00:03:16.291
he was just like, "I'm
ready to go, I'm hungry."

00:03:16.291 --> 00:03:18.543
- And then we had to shop for
the food we were gonna eat.

00:03:18.543 --> 00:03:19.639
- Yeah, and you should never

00:03:19.639 --> 00:03:20.643
grocery shop on a hungry stomach.

00:03:20.643 --> 00:03:22.679
- No, you shouldn't, but you know,

00:03:22.679 --> 00:03:23.943
you have to do what you have to do

00:03:23.943 --> 00:03:26.001
when you're handcuffed to your sister.

00:03:26.001 --> 00:03:27.567
- This is what Mama made, are you,

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:28.958
do I need to call up
our mother and be like,

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:30.263
"Ragu isn't good enough for Michael?"

00:03:30.263 --> 00:03:31.387
- [Michael] Is that what she uses?

00:03:31.387 --> 00:03:32.220
- Yes!

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.053
- [Michael] For everything?

00:03:33.053 --> 00:03:34.059
- For spaghetti!

00:03:34.059 --> 00:03:36.247
- You asked me what I wanted to eat.

00:03:36.247 --> 00:03:38.695
I said turkey meatballs, you said okay.

00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:40.163
- No, you said meatballs,

00:03:40.163 --> 00:03:42.465
and I was like, "Ooh, spaghetti
and meatballs, perfect."

00:03:42.465 --> 00:03:45.302
Spaghetti and turkey gravy
meatballs does not sound good.

00:03:45.302 --> 00:03:48.658
- First of all, the
recipe came recommended

00:03:48.658 --> 00:03:50.726
from my friend who is a chef.

00:03:50.726 --> 00:03:53.643
- But was it served with spaghetti?

00:03:54.838 --> 00:03:55.678
- It's a meatball.

00:03:55.678 --> 00:03:56.758
It's a meatball!
- No!

00:03:56.758 --> 00:03:59.982
- First of all, I'm
handcuffed to you for 24 hours

00:03:59.982 --> 00:04:02.396
and you can't give me two
tablespoons of turkey gravy

00:04:02.396 --> 00:04:03.690
on my recipe?

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:07.195
- I asked what you wanted to
eat when we went to Chipotle.

00:04:07.195 --> 00:04:08.758
- We cooked.
- We cooked.

00:04:08.758 --> 00:04:10.462
Key and Ryann came over
from Real Housewives.

00:04:10.462 --> 00:04:11.690
- [Michael] They did.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:12.523
- [Destinee] And we were tryin'

00:04:12.523 --> 00:04:13.356
to cook your meatballs and spaghettis.

00:04:13.356 --> 00:04:15.705
At first, it was nonsense and chaotic.

00:04:15.705 --> 00:04:16.681
(Michael laughs)

00:04:16.681 --> 00:04:17.717
But then, we figured like,

00:04:17.717 --> 00:04:19.065
"You work that half of the kitchen,

00:04:19.065 --> 00:04:20.821
"I work this half of the kitchen."

00:04:20.821 --> 00:04:21.654
- [Michael] Yeah.

00:04:21.654 --> 00:04:22.769
- [Destinee] And we kind of got it down.

00:04:22.769 --> 00:04:23.641
Food!

00:04:23.641 --> 00:04:24.474
- Hey!

00:04:24.474 --> 00:04:25.457
- Wine, housewives.

00:04:25.457 --> 00:04:27.181
(woman laughs)
(Destinee laughs)

00:04:27.181 --> 00:04:29.774
So, we're done hosting for the night

00:04:29.774 --> 00:04:32.034
and we have all of these dishes.

00:04:32.034 --> 00:04:34.614
I say we just put 'em in the dishwasher.

00:04:34.614 --> 00:04:37.134
- Great idea. (both laugh)

00:04:37.134 --> 00:04:38.394
I was so physically drained.

00:04:38.394 --> 00:04:39.938
And I ate a lot.

00:04:39.938 --> 00:04:42.653
So when I finally laid down, it was over.

00:04:42.653 --> 00:04:43.750
I was done.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.878
So the snap that you got was like this

00:04:45.878 --> 00:04:48.228
because that's how I sleep.

00:04:48.228 --> 00:04:50.228
- Dude, I, did we snore?

00:04:52.678 --> 00:04:54.626
(both laugh)

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:56.066
- My biggest thing going into this,

00:04:56.066 --> 00:04:59.802
I was like, "Michael is
always late doing something."

00:04:59.802 --> 00:05:00.658
- Hey, first of all--

00:05:00.658 --> 00:05:02.844
- It's always something.

00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:04.286
- I wouldn't say always.

00:05:04.286 --> 00:05:06.010
- We were late coming here!

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.458
- We were handcuffed together!

00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:11.470
You can't plan to start your day

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:13.343
like you normally start it,

00:05:13.343 --> 00:05:15.446
except now you're handcuffed to a person

00:05:15.446 --> 00:05:16.763
and have the same--
- You plan accordingly.

00:05:16.763 --> 00:05:18.190
- The same amount of, exactly.
- You plan,

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.038
okay, we're not going back down this road.

00:05:20.038 --> 00:05:20.903
- We're not doing that again.

00:05:20.903 --> 00:05:21.926
- We're not going back down this road.

00:05:21.926 --> 00:05:22.902
- Don't bring that up, stop being petty.

00:05:22.902 --> 00:05:24.282
- [Destinee] You still
had to come to my job

00:05:24.282 --> 00:05:25.406
and I went to your job.

00:05:25.406 --> 00:05:26.239
- [Michael] Yes.

00:05:26.239 --> 00:05:27.072
- [Destinee] So I had meetings

00:05:27.072 --> 00:05:28.036
that you had to be sitting in.

00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:28.869
- [Michael] That's pretty cool.

00:05:28.869 --> 00:05:29.702
- [Destinee] Yeah?

00:05:29.702 --> 00:05:30.664
- [Michael] It was.

00:05:30.664 --> 00:05:31.497
It was cool sitting in

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.460
and kind of seeing how it looks in here,

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.892
and there's all kinds
of stuff going on, and--

00:05:33.892 --> 00:05:34.956
- All right, so at the end of the--

00:05:34.956 --> 00:05:37.202
- So (laughs) don't try to
snap while I'm snappin'.

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:38.360
- (laughing) I'm trying to,

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.193
I'm trying to do this for my job.

00:05:39.193 --> 00:05:40.300
- Okay, it's all right, I'll let you go.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.438
- [Destinee] Sorry, excuse me. (laughs)

00:05:41.438 --> 00:05:42.638
- So we're roaming the BuzzFeed hallway

00:05:42.638 --> 00:05:44.757
and I'm just gonna interrupt
the video that she's doing--

00:05:44.757 --> 00:05:45.733
- Yes.

00:05:45.733 --> 00:05:46.825
- With my Snap Story.

00:05:46.825 --> 00:05:48.521
- I hope this is worth it for you.

00:05:48.521 --> 00:05:49.437
- This is worth it for me.

00:05:49.437 --> 00:05:50.276
- [Destinee] I hope this is worth it.

00:05:50.276 --> 00:05:51.597
- I been handcuffed to
you for the entire day

00:05:51.597 --> 00:05:52.778
and this is my will, okay?

00:05:52.778 --> 00:05:53.611
(Destinee laughs)

00:05:53.611 --> 00:05:54.444
You see this?

00:05:54.444 --> 00:05:55.661
I can't believe we're really doing this.

00:05:55.661 --> 00:05:57.024
- [Destinee] I felt the
same way going to your job.

00:05:57.024 --> 00:05:59.913
Like it was really cool
getting to see what you do

00:05:59.913 --> 00:06:01.157
and your side of things.

00:06:01.157 --> 00:06:03.704
But the whole us being
fluid thing didn't work

00:06:03.704 --> 00:06:05.597
when you were trying to deejay.

00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:08.177
- No, it doesn't, because you
don't know those movements

00:06:08.177 --> 00:06:11.101
and you don't know how
that whole situation works.

00:06:11.101 --> 00:06:12.737
I move a lot, I move quickly.

00:06:12.737 --> 00:06:14.143
- I definitely think this experience

00:06:14.143 --> 00:06:15.479
has made me appreciate you more.

00:06:15.479 --> 00:06:16.517
- Aw, that's sweet.

00:06:16.517 --> 00:06:18.597
- Before, I was just like,
"Oh yeah, this is my brother."

00:06:18.597 --> 00:06:21.105
I see that you have like
these different nuances

00:06:21.105 --> 00:06:22.977
and mannerisms that make you you

00:06:22.977 --> 00:06:24.737
that I didn't know were there before.

00:06:24.737 --> 00:06:26.133
- And vice versa, you know.

00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:28.911
You see that I get
aggressive when I'm hungry.

00:06:28.911 --> 00:06:30.215
(Michael laughs)

00:06:30.215 --> 00:06:32.677
But I also have a different
appreciation for you as well,

00:06:32.677 --> 00:06:35.016
and I kind of also get to see, you know,

00:06:35.016 --> 00:06:36.637
like what kind of woman you're becoming

00:06:36.637 --> 00:06:37.989
as you're getting older

00:06:37.989 --> 00:06:40.987
and starting your life
and starting your career.

00:06:40.987 --> 00:06:42.189
- [Destinee] Aw!

00:06:42.189 --> 00:06:43.285
- [Michael] So that's, it's cool

00:06:43.285 --> 00:06:44.376
to see where you're at right now,

00:06:44.376 --> 00:06:46.011
you know, where you're working.

00:06:46.011 --> 00:06:46.957
- He does love me!

00:06:46.957 --> 00:06:47.790
(Michael laughs)

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.623
Wouldn't do this again, though.

00:06:48.623 --> 00:06:49.456
- No, never again.

00:06:49.456 --> 00:06:50.289
- Wouldn't do this again.

00:06:50.289 --> 00:06:51.122
- You can call that a dub.

00:06:51.122 --> 00:06:51.955
- Are we done, 24 hours?

00:06:51.955 --> 00:06:52.788
- [Man] Yes.

00:06:52.788 --> 00:06:54.281
- All right, yes, absolutely.

00:06:54.281 --> 00:06:55.114
- Let's do this.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:55.947
- Absolutely, sis, I'm wonderful.

00:06:55.947 --> 00:06:57.720
Thank you, I'm good, bye.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:58.553
- Oh, yes!

00:06:59.773 --> 00:07:00.977
Here you go.

00:07:00.977 --> 00:07:02.749
- [Destinee] Free at last, free at last!

00:07:02.749 --> 00:07:05.499
(dramatic music)

00:07:11.192 --> 00:07:13.148
(logo whooshes)

00:07:13.148 --> 00:07:14.095
(hinge squeaks)

